Subject: [PATCH 0007] Relocate mutable engine globals into doom_ctx_t behind a constant address

The SBF loader refuses any writable static data (.data AND .bss,
measured M1006/M1021), so every mutable global becomes a field of one
context struct doom_ctx_t reached through the compile-time constant
DOOM_CTX (a real backing on the host, a pinned account-data address on
SBF with a runtime guard).  Immutable tables become const (.rodata).
Dead debug globals (info, profilecount) are removed with W_Profile.
The zone arena (Z_Init) lives inside the context at the measured 3 MiB
floor, 8-byte aligned via a union so the memzone_t header is aligned
on host and SBF alike (UBSan backstop over the full DEMO1 replay).
Pointer-array initializers (player_names) assign each element at
runtime: a static table of string addresses would need .data relocs.

This patch is generated, not hand-written: stunts/doom-host/tools/mkctx.py
<linuxdoom-1.10-dir> (with tools/doom_ctx_spec.json) reproduces it
byte-for-byte from the 0001-0006 tree.  Names with no
struct-member/param/local collision get #define N (DOOM_CTX->N);
colliding struct members are renamed _m (member accesses are unambiguous
x->N); a few bare uses become (DOOM_CTX->N) with no define; shadowing
locals are renamed.  states/mobjinfo stay mutable: the -fast/nightmare
path writes states[].tics and mobjinfo[].speed (measured).

Golden-neutral on the host: DEMO1 DOOM-FB1 stream
2db988a2fa58c294d070fc9e2e6a52de615a8aa4b13ec9af33056985189d69c2 over
5,026 tics byte-identical; DOOM-ST1 S0 unchanged; one full ASan+UBSan
replay with zero reports.  Per-tic state hashes agree except tics
2291-3892, a pre-existing harness property (uninitialized plat->count
read by the retained encoder; identical binaries disagree with
themselves there run-to-run).

Applies on top of 0001-0006.

